1
00:00:00,467 --> 00:00:06,067
What if, right now, you could see exactly what was going to happen in

2
00:00:06,067 --> 00:00:12,633
the next 10 seconds? What would you do? Avoid an embarrassing fall? Prevent an

3
00:00:12,633 --> 00:00:16,167
accident? Find out what your crush is about to say? Or, use those

4
00:00:16,167 --> 00:00:22,133
10 seconds to change something you might regret for the rest of your life?

5
00:00:22,233 --> 00:00:25,400
It sounds like a pretty small superpower, but

6
00:00:25,400 --> 00:00:29,633
think about it. Ten seconds can sometimes change everything.

7
00:00:30,267 --> 00:00:34,967
The rule is simple. Whenever you focus and blink, you can see exactly 10

8
00:00:34,967 --> 00:00:39,333
seconds into the future. Not a feeling. Not a prediction. You actually see

9
00:00:39,333 --> 00:00:43,767
what is about to happen, then, you return to the present, and you

10
00:00:43,900 --> 00:00:50,900
have 10 seconds to decide: let that future happen, or try to change it.

11
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:55,167
At first? You would obviously use this incredible power for

12
00:00:55,167 --> 00:01:00,100
the most important things in life. Like, not embarrassing yourself.

13
00:01:00,733 --> 00:01:03,767
You see yourself trip, and somehow, the entire cup of coffee

14
00:01:03,767 --> 00:01:07,400
ends up all over your clothes. Even worse, someone nearby is

15
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,733
already holding a phone. No, the internet does not need another meme

16
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:18,667
today. You return to the present. Step slightly to the left.

17
00:01:18,733 --> 00:01:24,567
Avoid the crack. Perfect. You smile confidently. Having a superpower

18
00:01:24,567 --> 00:01:28,033
feels amazing, then, you walk straight into a pole.

19
00:01:28,033 --> 00:01:32,167
BONK! Apparently, seeing the future still cannot save your dignity.

20
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:36,267
During a meeting, you suddenly see your boss calling your

21
00:01:36,267 --> 00:01:40,167
name. You have exactly 10 seconds. Your brain instantly enters

22
00:01:40,167 --> 00:01:44,467
emergency mode. You open the document. Scan the most important

23
00:01:44,467 --> 00:01:47,867
line. Ten seconds later, "What do you think?" You sit

24
00:01:47,867 --> 00:01:53,100
up straight. Stay calm, and give a surprisingly intelligent answer.

25
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:58,367
Everyone nods. Your boss looks impressed. Congratulations. You just used

26
00:01:58,367 --> 00:02:02,000
a supernatural ability to look like someone, who was

27
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:07,333
actually paying attention during the meeting, and honestly, that

28
00:02:07,333 --> 00:02:10,267
might be one of the best uses of this power.

29
00:02:10,933 --> 00:02:15,133
Sometimes the power would help with much smaller things. You see

30
00:02:15,133 --> 00:02:18,333
your phone about to fall off the table. The screen hits

31
00:02:18,333 --> 00:02:23,600
the floor. Shatters. You return to the present. Calmly reach out your

32
00:02:23,600 --> 00:02:28,033
hand. The cat pushes the phone, and, you catch it. Perfect.

33
00:02:28,100 --> 00:02:33,067
Your superpower just saved you a few hundred dollars in repairs,

34
00:02:33,067 --> 00:02:36,867
but from this point on, things start getting much more serious.

35
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:41,800
You are about to cross the street. The light is green. Everything

36
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:45,967
looks completely normal, then you blink, and see, a vehicle speeding

37
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:48,833
out from a blind corner. If you keep moving, you are

38
00:02:48,833 --> 00:02:56,067
going to collide. You return to the present, and stop. One second.

39
00:02:56,333 --> 00:03:00,533
Two seconds. Three. The vehicle actually flies past you. Only

40
00:03:00,533 --> 00:03:03,667
a few feet away, and for the first time, you

41
00:03:03,667 --> 00:03:08,000
realize something. This power is not just useful for avoiding embarrassing

42
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:12,833
moments. It could save your life. Maybe even someone else's.

43
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:17,233
And of course, you would immediately think about sports. During a game,

44
00:03:17,233 --> 00:03:20,300
you see your opponent move to the right. Easy. You return to

45
00:03:20,300 --> 00:03:23,033
the present, and move right before he even makes his move, but

46
00:03:23,033 --> 00:03:30,667
there is a problem. He sees you move, so he changes direction.

47
00:03:30,733 --> 00:03:33,967
Left. Wait. That is not what you saw, and that

48
00:03:33,967 --> 00:03:38,500
is when you discover the biggest problem with your power. The

49
00:03:38,500 --> 00:03:41,967
future is not fixed. The moment you change what you do,

50
00:03:41,967 --> 00:03:45,633
the future changes too. Every decision creates a different outcome.

51
00:03:46,833 --> 00:03:51,167
During a job interview, you see the next question. "What

52
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:55,333
is your biggest weakness?" You have 10 seconds to prepare. This

53
00:03:55,333 --> 00:04:01,833
time, no awkward silence. No panic. You deliver the perfect answer.

54
00:04:01,833 --> 00:04:06,000
The interviewer smiles, but then you look 10 seconds ahead

55
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:09,467
again, and hear him ask: "Did you prepare that answer

56
00:04:09,467 --> 00:04:14,300
beforehand?", Okay. Maybe this power cannot save you from every interview.

57
00:04:14,933 --> 00:04:19,133
But some things are much harder. You are standing in front of

58
00:04:19,133 --> 00:04:22,633
someone you have liked for months. The words have been stuck in

59
00:04:22,633 --> 00:04:28,100
your head forever. You blink, and see her reaction. "I'm sorry, "

60
00:04:28,100 --> 00:04:33,267
Your heart drops. Now you have a choice. You could stay silent.

61
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:38,967
Say nothing. Never get rejected. Never feel the pain, but then you start

62
00:04:38,967 --> 00:04:44,667
thinking, if you avoid every future you do not like, are you really living?

63
00:04:44,667 --> 00:04:48,967
You take a breath, and say it anyway. "I like you." She pauses,

64
00:04:48,967 --> 00:04:55,500
then, "I'm sorry. I'm just not ready for a relationship." Exactly what you saw,

65
00:04:55,500 --> 00:05:00,700
but this time, you smile, because at least now, you have an answer.

66
00:05:00,867 --> 00:05:03,767
Some futures do not need to be changed.

67
00:05:03,767 --> 00:05:08,767
Sometimes, you just need enough courage to face them.

68
00:05:09,467 --> 00:05:14,300
Then one day, those 10 seconds really change you. Your phone

69
00:05:14,300 --> 00:05:19,333
starts ringing. It is your mom. You are busy. You think: "

70
00:05:19,333 --> 00:05:24,467
I'll call her back later." Your finger moves toward the decline button,

71
00:05:24,467 --> 00:05:27,567
but out of habit, you look 10 seconds into the future.

72
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:32,533
You see yourself rejecting the call. Walking forward, and behind you, an

73
00:05:32,533 --> 00:05:36,200
elderly man steps into the road. A truck is coming straight

74
00:05:36,200 --> 00:05:40,367
toward him. You return to the present. You do not think.

75
00:05:40,367 --> 00:05:47,133
You run. Grab the man. Pull him backward. The truck flies past.

76
00:05:47,267 --> 00:05:52,233
Missing both of you by inches. You are breathing hard. The man does

77
00:05:52,233 --> 00:05:57,600
not even understand what just happened. You just saved someone's life, then, your

78
00:05:57,600 --> 00:06:03,600
phone vibrates again. Your mom is still calling. You answer. "Mom?" There is a

79
00:06:03,600 --> 00:06:09,200
brief silence, then she simply asks: "Did you eat yet?" That is it.

80
00:06:09,333 --> 00:06:15,667
No emergency. No terrible news. No dramatic final words. Just an

81
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:20,167
ordinary question. The kind of question you might ignore every

82
00:06:20,167 --> 00:06:24,967
day. You laugh. "Yeah, Mom. I already ate." You talk for

83
00:06:24,967 --> 00:06:30,333
a few minutes. Nothing dramatic happens, but suddenly, you realize something.

84
00:06:30,333 --> 00:06:34,233
You spent the entire day staring 10 seconds into the

85
00:06:34,233 --> 00:06:38,867
future, and nearly ignored someone who was with you, right now.

86
00:06:39,567 --> 00:06:42,867
You thought the greatest part of your power, was knowing what would

87
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:47,000
happen next, but it was not, because even if you can see

88
00:06:47,100 --> 00:06:53,733
10 seconds ahead, you still do not know what happens in 10 minutes.

89
00:06:53,733 --> 00:06:58,200
Tomorrow. Next year, or when the last time you see someone, will

90
00:06:58,200 --> 00:07:04,133
actually be, and maybe, that is exactly what gives life its meaning.

91
00:07:04,867 --> 00:07:08,867
Of course, seeing 10 seconds into the future is only a thought experiment.

92
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:14,633
It is not something we can actually do. In real life, there is

93
00:07:14,633 --> 00:07:20,133
no rewind button. No warning screen. No countdown telling us that an

94
00:07:20,133 --> 00:07:26,333
important moment is about to happen, but maybe, we do not need one.

95
00:07:26,467 --> 00:07:30,767
You can still look before crossing the street. You can still say

96
00:07:30,767 --> 00:07:36,433
what you really feel. You can call your parents. Apologize to

97
00:07:36,433 --> 00:07:41,200
someone. Thank someone. Hold someone you love for a little longer,

98
00:07:41,200 --> 00:07:46,133
and sometimes, small decisions like those are enough to change the future.

99
00:07:46,267 --> 00:07:48,900
You do not need to see 10 seconds ahead to live a

100
00:07:48,900 --> 00:07:53,233
better life. You just need to stop wasting, the 10 seconds you have

101
00:07:53,233 --> 00:07:58,000
right now. "The future can wait. This moment can't." If you really could

102
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:04,600
see 10 seconds into the future, what would you use it for?
